---
import PolicySection from "./PolicySection.astro";
import { ul } from "./styles";
---

<PolicySection title="What we collect">
  <ul class:list={ul}>
    <li>
      <strong class="text-foreground">Your account:</strong> your e-mail address, a hash of your password kept by our
      sign-in provider, Supabase Auth (the app itself never stores your password), and when you signed up and last
      signed in.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong class="text-foreground">With "Continue with Google":</strong> the name, e-mail address and profile picture
      that Google shares. The app uses only the e-mail address.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong class="text-foreground">Your sessions:</strong> for each signed-in session, the IP address and the browser
      you use (user agent), plus a security log of account events (such as sign-ins) with the IP address, kept by
      Supabase Auth.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong class="text-foreground">What you create:</strong> your group's name, task titles (free text, so please
      keep anything sensitive out of them), memberships, the tasks you join and the days or weeks you mark done.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong class="text-foreground">Technical data:</strong>
      <ul class:list={ul}>
        <li>our own log entries: the route, your user id, a request id and the time;</li>
        <li>
          error reports, which identify you only by your user id and never contain cookies, headers, request bodies or
          query strings;
        </li>
        <li>our own log entries and error reports mask e-mail addresses and invite codes;</li>
        <li>
          Cloudflare, which hosts the site, processes your IP address and request details to serve it, and its request
          logs record each address you request (an invite link contains its code) with request details such as your IP
          address.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li>No analytics, no advertising and no tracking scripts.</li>
  </ul>
</PolicySection>
